3. Run the command `stap -g [filename-from-step-1].stp` as root. Note that if the host is rebooted, the changes will be lost, and the script must be run again.

4. Alternatively, build the SystemTap script on a development system with `stap -g -p`.

5. Another mitigation method is to install the `kmod-tpe` package from ELRepo. This package provides the Trusted Path Execution (TPE) kernel module, which denies users from executing programs that are not owned by root or are writable. This module works out of the box with no configuration and blocks the known exploit.

